# =========================================================================
# Quadratus configuration
# Copy this file to .env. The defaults assume subscription transport, so on
# a machine with the three CLIs installed and signed in, an empty .env works.
# =========================================================================

# --- Transport: subscription (CLI) vs billed API -------------------------
# "cli"  drives the vendor coding-agent CLI you are already signed into with
#        your consumer subscription (claude / codex / grok). No API key and
#        no per-token billing; usage draws on the subscription's rate-limit
#        window instead. This is the default, and the reason this project
#        exists.
# "api"  uses the billed HTTP SDK and needs the matching key below.
#
# A provider whose CLI is missing reports itself unavailable rather than
# quietly moving onto billed transport -- an unexpected invoice is a worse
# failure than a clear error.
#
# Install once per provider (verified on macOS, 2026-09-12):
#   npm install -g @anthropic-ai/claude-code     -> claude
#   npm install -g @openai/codex                 -> codex
#   brew install --cask grok-build               -> grok
#
# Then sign in once, each in its own browser flow:
#   claude          -> run it, then /login       (Claude Pro/Max)
#   codex login     -> check with `codex login status`  (ChatGPT Plus/Pro)
#   grok login      -> `grok models` then lists what your account can reach
# LLM_BACKEND=cli
#
# Per-provider overrides, so you can mix (e.g. Claude on subscription, Grok
# on an API key because the CLI is not installed).
# CLAUDE_BACKEND=cli
# OPENAI_BACKEND=cli
# GROK_BACKEND=api
#
# IMPORTANT: subscription transport authenticates as *you*. Routing anyone
# else's prompts through it violates the consumer terms of every vendor
# here. The project GUI also has filesystem and command access, so public
# Gradio sharing is disabled on every backend. Keep it local and single-user.

# --- Before your first run -----------------------------------------------
#   quadratus --status   free: what is configured and what each model
#                        resolves to today
#   quadratus --probe    spends a little budget: asks each installed CLI
#                        which aliases it actually accepts, and caches the
#                        answers (~/.quadratus/aliases.json)
#
# All three flag sets have been exercised by signed-in calls (claude 2.1.269,
# codex-cli 0.154.0, grok 1.0.30). A later CLI release can still rename a
# flag. If a vendor's calls fail, the fix is usually one flag and it belongs
# here rather than in the source:
# QUADRATUS_CLI_BINARY_OPENAI=codex
# QUADRATUS_CLI_ARGS_OPENAI=
# QUADRATUS_CLI_BINARY_GROK=grok
# QUADRATUS_CLI_ARGS_GROK=

# --- API keys (only needed for providers set to the "api" backend) -------
# Left commented out on purpose: a copied placeholder is a set key, and the
# default subscription transport needs none. Uncomment only the ones you use.
# Anthropic (Claude): https://console.anthropic.com/
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=your_anthropic_key_here

# OpenAI (ChatGPT): https://platform.openai.com/api-keys
# OPENAI_API_KEY=your_openai_key_here

# xAI (Grok): https://console.x.ai/
# Either XAI_API_KEY or GROK_API_KEY is accepted.
# XAI_API_KEY=your_xai_key_here

# --- Model selection (optional) ------------------------------------------
# Dated model IDs for the "api" backend. An API takes no aliases, so these
# pin a release and go stale on their own schedule -- override to match what
# your accounts can reach.
# CLAUDE_MODEL=claude-opus-5
# OPENAI_MODEL=gpt-5.6-sol
# GROK_MODEL=grok-4.6
#
# On the "cli" backend, models are addressed by the CLI's own alias, and the
# orchestrator seats deliberately address a model *line* rather than a
# release so a run follows the line forward on its own. Override any one
# model's alias when a vendor ships something the table has not caught up
# with -- this beats both the probe cache and the built-in seed:
# QUADRATUS_ALIAS_CLAUDE_FABLE=fable
# QUADRATUS_ALIAS_OPENAI_GPT_6_ASTRA=gpt-6-astra
# QUADRATUS_ALIAS_CLAUDE_OPUS=opus
#
# Where the probe cache lives, if you want it somewhere else:
# QUADRATUS_ALIAS_CACHE=~/.quadratus/aliases.json
#
# Claude's safety classifiers can decline a request outright: the API returns
# HTTP 200 with stop_reason "refusal" and no content (Claude API since Opus
# 4.7, every Fable / Mythos model). Set a fallback and the same request is
# re-sent once to that model; leave it empty and the refusal surfaces as an
# error. Anthropic's permitted server-side fallback targets for Fable are
# claude-opus-4-8 and claude-opus-5. Use a full model ID for the API backend
# and the CLI's own alias for the CLI backend. Only the code discussion
# pipeline uses it: the session engine never swaps the model behind a seat,
# so there a refusal always surfaces.
# CLAUDE_REFUSAL_FALLBACK_MODEL=
# CLAUDE_CLI_REFUSAL_FALLBACK_MODEL=

# --- Collaboration behaviour (optional) ----------------------------------
# Order in which providers take roles: the first is the lead implementer,
# the rest are reviewers/refiners.
# PROVIDER_ORDER=claude,openai,grok
# Number of review/refinement rounds (higher = more thorough, slower, pricier).
# ROUNDS=1
# Which provider performs the final synthesis ("lead" uses the first provider).
# SYNTHESIZER=lead

# --- CLI model tiers (optional, "cli" backend only) ----------------------
# CLI backends address models by the CLI's own alias, not a dated API ID.
# Two tiers are read per provider. Only "high" is used today: it is the model
# the code discussion pipeline calls. Nothing requests the "low" tier yet, so
# setting it changes nothing; the session engine names its seats by roster
# key and takes its aliases from QUADRATUS_ALIAS_* above.
# Both GROK_CLI_MODEL_* values are empty on purpose: no model flag is sent, so
# the grok CLI applies its own current default and the seat follows whatever
# xAI ships. Set one only to pin that tier against the vendor's choice.
# CLAUDE_CLI_MODEL_HIGH=opus
# CLAUDE_CLI_MODEL_LOW=haiku
# OPENAI_CLI_MODEL_HIGH=gpt-5.6-sol
# OPENAI_CLI_MODEL_LOW=gpt-5.6-luna
# GROK_CLI_MODEL_HIGH=
# GROK_CLI_MODEL_LOW=

# --- Request tuning (optional) -------------------------------------------
# MAX_TOKENS=8000
# REQUEST_TIMEOUT=600
# CLI calls run a whole agent loop, not one completion, so they need a much
# more generous ceiling than an HTTP request.
# CLI_TIMEOUT=900
# MAX_RETRIES=4
# RETRY_BASE_DELAY=2

# --- GUI / file handling (optional) --------------------------------------
# MAX_MEMORY_ENTRIES=10
# MAX_FILE_BYTES=1048576
# MAX_FILE_CHARS=20000
